Aim:
To develop and execute a Java Applet program to draw a human face using the Graphics class.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Import the Applet and Graphics classes.
3. Create a class that extends Applet.
4. Override the paint() method.
5. Draw the face, eyes, nose, mouth, and hair using graphics methods.
6. Compile and run the applet.
7. Stop.

Program:
import java.applet.Applet;
import java.awt.Graphics;
import java.awt.Color;

public class HumanFace extends Applet {

    public void paint(Graphics g) {
        // Draw face
        g.setColor(Color.YELLOW);
        g.fillOval(100, 50, 200, 220);

        // Draw hair
        g.setColor(Color.BLACK);
        g.fillArc(100, 40, 200, 100, 0, 180);

        // Draw eyes
        g.fillOval(145, 120, 25, 25);
        g.fillOval(230, 120, 25, 25);

        // Draw nose
        g.drawLine(200, 140, 185, 180);
        g.drawLine(185, 180, 205, 180);

        // Draw mouth
        g.setColor(Color.RED);
        g.drawArc(155, 185, 90, 45, 180, 180);

        // Draw ears
        g.setColor(Color.YELLOW);
        g.fillOval(85, 125, 25, 50);
        g.fillOval(290, 125, 25, 50);

        // Draw neck
        g.fillRect(175, 260, 50, 45);

        // Draw body
        g.setColor(Color.BLUE);
        g.fillOval(120, 295, 160, 100);
    }
}



